# Qt 6 Quick / QML Rules

- Always use unversioned Qt 6 imports (`import QtQuick`, `import QtQuick.Layouts`, `import QtQuick.Templates as T`, `import QtQuick.Effects`).
- Declare `pragma ComponentBehavior: Bound` in files with delegates/popups and add explicit `required property` declarations inside every delegate. Qualify delegate properties via the delegate root `id`.
- Inside `RowLayout` / `ColumnLayout`, use `Layout.preferredWidth` and `Layout.preferredHeight` rather than raw `width` / `height`.
- Reuse `StudioIcon`, `StudioButton`, `StudioSwitch`, `StudioSlider`, `StudioScrollBar`, `StudioCard`, `StudioBadge`, and `Theme` tokens (`Dark` & `Light` booth modes) instead of ad-hoc inline styling.
- Wrap every user-visible string in a plain literal `qsTr("...")`, use `Font.DemiBold` (not `Font.SemiBold`), and verify `cmake --build --preset <preset> --target kmedia_qmllint` finishes with zero warnings.
- Preserve all three responsive breakpoints (`Wide >= 1080`, `Medium 680-1079`, `Compact < 680` down to `360x520`).
